{#- Générateur synthétique du cas d'usage « estimation de prix immobilier » (famille regression). -#}
"""Synthetic data generator — {{ spec.data.title }}.

Business scenario
    {{ wrap(business.context, 96, indent=4) }}

How the data is built
    The generator does **not** draw columns independently. It builds a latent property profile
    first (district, era, size, energy performance), derives every observable column from it, and
    finally computes the price through an explicit **multiplicative model in log-price**:

    * each characteristic contributes a factor (district premium, concave surface effect, energy
      penalty, floor x elevator interaction, transport accessibility, declared condition);
    * a mild market drift and a spring seasonality make ``listing_date`` genuinely informative;
    * the target is heteroscedastic by construction (absolute error grows with the price), which is
      what makes MAPE / median error more honest than RMSE alone;
    * irreducible log-normal noise keeps the achievable {{ spec.metrics.primary }} realistic;
    * a few legitimate prestige outliers and deliberate missing values exercise the preprocessing.

Determinism
    ``generate()`` is a pure function of ``(n_samples, seed, options)``: two runs produce the
    same bytes, which is what makes stack-to-stack comparisons meaningful.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

from pathlib import Path
from typing import Any, ClassVar, Mapping, Sequence

import numpy as np
import pandas as pd

from src.data.schemas import RawDataSchema
from src.utils.io import write_json, write_table_multiple
from src.utils.logging import get_logger
from src.utils.paths import ProjectPaths

logger = get_logger(__name__)

#: Default dataset name (overridable through the constructor / Hydra config).
DEFAULT_DATASET_NAME = "{{ spec.data.dataset_name }}"

